WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.683
Every launch needs a walkthrough. Nobody enjoys making it.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.949
Write the script.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:06.980
Record the screen.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.919
Retake. Retake.

5
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:08.996
Record the voice.

6
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:09.978
Sync the captions.

7
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.586
Then the product changes, and the walkthrough is already out of date.

8
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.773
The agent says done. The application records what really happened.

9
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.313
Seventy-six said success. The app disagreed.

10
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.722
No repro. Just flaky.

11
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.009
Meet Walkcast.

12
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.741
Paste a link. Get a narrated video walkthrough of your website.

13
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.526
Confirm you're authorized to test the site, then press record.

14
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.679
A real browser opens the site and clicks through its pages.

15
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.491
The narration follows what actually happened.

16
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.265
Captions. Chapters. Transcript.

17
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.248
At a CAPTCHA or two-factor prompt, Walkcast stops.

18
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.076
Choose natural offline Kokoro, a cloud voice, or record your own.

19
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.103
Same recorder.

20
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.254
Second job.

21
00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.192
Walkcast Lab turns failed browser-agent runs into regression tests.

22
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.812
Capture the failure. Classify the cause. Freeze it. Replay it.

23
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.800
Causes come from the app's recorded state, not an LLM judge.

24
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.471
Did the next version fix it, or break something else? Now you know.

25
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:14.959
Real browser.

26
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:16.870
Real state.

27
00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.029
Real evidence.

28
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.171
Walkcast. Show what actually happened. Free and open source. Visit our website.

